interp="""The survey finds that the spectral content of the dataset is dominated by only a handful of lines: HCN and HCO+ 2-1/3-2/4-3 (very high S/N at both nuclei), CS 7-6 (N 15 sigma, S 7.5 sigma, Xb47), a CH3OH J_-1-J_0 E blend in Band 5, and the blue wing of CO 3-2 at the Xb47 spw20 edge. Everything else (SO 5_6-4_5, 253.97 GHz bump, HC3N 28-27, HC15N, SO 8_8-7_7, HCN-vib, H13CN) is absent or only marginal, so shock/chemistry diagnostics beyond CS, HCN/HCO+ ratios and CH3OH will be limits (Q4, Q5). The proposal's SO(6_5-5_4) is not in the data. The system is resolved at 0.25-1": N (double-horned, broad, extended continuum), S (compact continuum, line centre ~65 km/s blueward of systemic, narrower), a narrow Bridge component 1.4" S of N, two eastern clumps (E1, E2, redshifted 50-90 km/s), a western clump, and a blue-shifted blob (Sblue) 3" S-SW of S with a broad (120-230 km/s) blue-shifted profile and a blue wing; the S nucleus itself has a 4-9% blue wing. These match the picture of a dense-gas outflow near the S nucleus, but the high-velocity channels are outside the clean mask, so wing fluxes are lower limits/dirty. N and S are cleanly separable at Bands 6-7 (beam minor axes 2.7-3.5" << 5.2") and only partially in Band 5. HCN/HCO+ at matched J is already a regional discriminator (N 0.6-1.0, S 0.4-0.5 at J=3-2); this is handed to Q1 together with matched-beam convolution. The delivered mfs/cont images are line-free."""
cav=["Formal errors only; channel noise is correlated (lag-1 rho ~0.1-0.5), approximately corrected; no flux-scale uncertainty (10% typical) and no primary-beam model check (pbcor correctness at region E1 ~7\" from phase centre, pb~0.7 in Band 6, not verified).",
"Double-horned profiles at N: single-Gaussian fits are poor (chi2r up to 20); use the 2G or integrated numbers. Gaussian centroids at S differ between beams (2764 at 5.7\" vs 2710 at 0.25\") because the beam mixes components.",
"High-velocity wings are outside the pipeline clean mask (0-7% of wing channels masked): wing fluxes are uncleaned and may be biased; the Sblue structure and S blue wing need confirmation (e.g. in the manual/tapered cubes, Q2/Q8).",
"Peak-pixel regions are defined on HCO+ 3-2 moment maps of Xb4d; apertures for E1/E2/W/Sblue/Bridge exist only for the 1\" and 0.25\" arrays, lower resolution cubes blend them into N/S.",
"Line IDs are from the Splatalogue rest frequencies at one systemic velocity; blends with line separation < line width (HCN v2=1, CS/H2CS/29SiO, CH3OH series, H13CN/CO) cannot be resolved with the data; the NS assignment of the 253.97 GHz bump is disfavoured but no alternative simple species fits.",
"Weak-line limits use the HCN/HCO+ profile of the same region as template; real profiles of other species may differ (narrower => limit in Jy/beam km/s is conservative).",
"Distance 40 Mpc (Pereira-Santaella+2024), literature only; not measured here.",
"CO 3-2 is only partially covered; its wing amplitude depends on the band edge and no CO baseline exists, so H13CN opacity (Q4) cannot be constrained in this file; confirmation would need data covering 345.3-345.8 GHz rest."]
rep=dict(datasets=datasets,recipe=recipe,results=R,interpretation=interp,caveats=cav)
json.dump(rep,open('/output/report.json','w'),indent=1)
